35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The closeout files are sobering. Catalogue-style awards still draw users a decade later. Mechanism-focused ones often stall.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The staffing rolls are alarming. Most phenotyping technicians left for industry. Modelling applicants are plentiful, though.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks. One engineer covers three institutes. That is a critical failure point.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The computing agreement covers simulation for free. But animal-unit day rates rose sharply after the vivarium rebuild.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,The incident logs match Victoria's concern. The shared instrumentation is a major source of interruption.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, if the technicians are gone, does that make the field-based projects riskier?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, yes. The glasshouse crew is full strength, but the technical support for phenotyping is thin.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, the free computing is a relief, but the animal facility costs are a hidden trap.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, exactly. The agency absorbs the compute, but the awardee pays the premium for animal care.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, the station records show field sites lost seasons to weather. Indoor holding rooms were fine.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"So, projects relying on live breeding or field work carry higher schedule risk.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"And projects relying on modelling have the people, but the infrastructure for spectroscopy is fragile.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,We must avoid anything that depends heavily on the broken spectroscopy suite or the expensive animal units.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The grant should favor work that leverages the free computing and the stable glasshouse crew.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,We should also avoid field sites that are prone to weather interruptions.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"The data points to a clear preference for stable, computational, or indoor biological work.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The human capital is there for modelling, but not for hands-on phenotyping.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"The infrastructure supports computation and glasshouse work, but not heavy animal or spectroscopy use.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,The cost structure favors computation and glasshouse over animal units and field travel.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"The interruptions are least likely in controlled, indoor, or computational environments.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
