60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Candidate A is greenhouse-based. The crew is full strength. It fits the stable profile.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate B uses live breeding. The schedule overruns are high. The technicians are scarce.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Candidate C uses spectroscopy. The suite is idle and under-staffed. High risk of interruption.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D is field-based. The station records show weather losses. Travel costs are rising.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,Candidate A avoids the field interruptions and the animal cost spikes. It seems the safest bet.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, do you agree that B is too risky given the staffing gaps?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, yes. The phenotyping technicians are gone. B will struggle to execute.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, is the cost of D's field work prohibitive now?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the travel lines are frozen, but the field sites are unreliable. The risk is operational, not just financial.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, A seems to align with all our concerns. Stable crew, no major infrastructure failures.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,A is the only one that doesn't hit a known failure point.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,B and D have human and environmental risks. C has infrastructure risk.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,C is the most dangerous due to the spectroscopy downtime.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,A leverages the stable glasshouse and avoids the animal cost spike.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,A is the most resilient to the interruptions we identified.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am convinced. A is the choice.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I concur. The staffing supports it.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,The infrastructure can handle it.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,The cost structure favors it.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,It avoids the known interruptions. I agree.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
